## Reading the Lab Code

<div style="line-height: 2;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;">Your students' Python lab uses four things they haven't met in a lesson: an import from a file the course wrote, the <code style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1; padding: 0 4px;">abs</code> function, models written as functions, and functions passed into other functions. Step through a similar program here so none of it catches you off guard.</div>
